--- !u!114 &672820200843344298
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 7424024454683550127}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 048f975937bfbbb46b1f990f001dd74b, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  nerdImage: {fileID: 8594728884818308614}
  idleFrame: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 684eae82a407b0242aab850f89d7d0a8, type: 3}
  talkFrame: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c39ac9004182b8244896c1203922ac92, type: 3}
  factText: {fileID: 8804683650176456865}
  lettersPerSecond: 40
  mouthSpeed: 8
  facts:
  - Snails have thousands of small teeth on their radula for cutting up food.
  - Almost all snails are "right handed", meaning their shell curves the same way
    as your right hand.
  - Most snails are hermaphrodites! They possess both male and female reproductive
    organs.
  - There are species of snails found in almost all habitats! From deep ocean trenches
    to barren deserts. Even in Antarctica!
  - There are over <b>40,000</b> species of snails!
  - The smallest known snail is the sea snail <b><i>Ammonicera minortalis</i></b>,
    measuring just about 0.012 inches.
  - The top speed of a common garden snail is about <b>0.03</b> miles per hour.
  - The scientific name for a snail, <b><i>Gastropoda</i></b>, means "Stomach foot".
  - The Scaly-foot Gastropod, or the <b><i>Volcano Snail</i></b>, lives 8,200 feet
    below sea level, and has an iron-plated shell layered with pyrite.
  - The largest species of snail in the world is the giant African land snail. It
    can measure up to <b>15 inches</b> and weigh up to <b>2.2 lbs</b>!
  - When snails hibernate, they seal themselves inside their shells with a mucus
    plug. They can stay there for <b>months</b> or even <b>years</b>!
  - Snails are nocturnal, and usually move about at night.
  - A typical snail sleep cycle lasts for <b>2-4 days</b>. Then they stay awake for
    a little over a day, before going back to sleep.
  - Snails are not insects but mollusks, like slugs, clams and squid.
  - Snails have no ears and are completely deaf.
  - Snails can be herbivores, carnivores and omnivores. Some even eat decaying matter
    and other snails!
  - Take me to snurch!
